// MARK: - Tarot Upright Meanings
"The Fool represents the spirit of adventure and the beginning of a new journey, embodying pure potential and innocence. This card encourages you to embrace the unknown with an open heart, trusting that the universe will guide you. Symbolically, the Fool steps off a cliff, carrying only a small knapsack, reminding us that we don't need to carry the weight of the past to move forward. In everyday life, this might manifest as starting a new job, moving to a new city, or embarking on a personal quest for self-discovery, where faith in oneself leads to unexpected growth and opportunities.\n\nPractically, the Fool urges you to take calculated risks rather than playing it safe all the time. It highlights the importance of spontaneity in breaking free from routine, fostering creativity and joy. Whether in relationships or career, this card suggests approaching situations with a beginner's mind, free from preconceptions, which can lead to innovative solutions and deeper connections." = "The Fool represents the spirit of adventure and the beginning of a new journey, embodying pure potential and innocence. This card encourages you to embrace the unknown with an open heart, trusting that the universe will guide you. Symbolically, the Fool steps off a cliff, carrying only a small knapsack, reminding us that we don't need to carry the weight of the past to move forward. In everyday life, this might manifest as starting a new job, moving to a new city, or embarking on a personal quest for self-discovery, where faith in oneself leads to unexpected growth and opportunities.\n\nPractically, the Fool urges you to take calculated risks rather than playing it safe all the time. It highlights the importance of spontaneity in breaking free from routine, fostering creativity and joy. Whether in relationships or career, this card suggests approaching situations with a beginner's mind, free from preconceptions, which can lead to innovative solutions and deeper connections.";

"The Magician symbolizes manifestation, resourcefulness, and the power of will to turn ideas into reality. With one hand pointing to the heavens and the other to the earth, he channels divine energy into practical action, reminding us that we possess all the tools needed for success. This card often appears when you're at a point of harnessing your skills and talents to create something meaningful, such as launching a project or pursuing a passion.\n\nIn everyday contexts, the Magician encourages focused intention and skillful execution. Whether negotiating a deal, learning a new skill, or improving relationships, it highlights your ability to influence outcomes through confidence and adaptability. Spiritually, it represents alignment between mind, body, and spirit, urging you to act as a conduit for positive change in your life and others'." = "The Magician symbolizes manifestation, resourcefulness, and the power of will to turn ideas into reality. With one hand pointing to the heavens and the other to the earth, he channels divine energy into practical action, reminding us that we possess all the tools needed for success. This card often appears when you're at a point of harnessing your skills and talents to create something meaningful, such as launching a project or pursuing a passion.\n\nIn everyday contexts, the Magician encourages focused intention and skillful execution. Whether negotiating a deal, learning a new skill, or improving relationships, it highlights your ability to influence outcomes through confidence and adaptability. Spiritually, it represents alignment between mind, body, and spirit, urging you to act as a conduit for positive change in your life and others'.";

// MARK: - Zodiac Descriptions
"Aries thrives on speed and excitement, while Taurus prefers stability and slow growth. Taurus might find Aries reckless, and Aries may see Taurus as too rigid. However, if Aries respects Taurus' need for security and Taurus accepts Aries' need for freedom, they can balance each other." = "Aries thrives on speed and excitement, while Taurus prefers stability and slow growth. Taurus might find Aries reckless, and Aries may see Taurus as too rigid. However, if Aries respects Taurus' need for security and Taurus accepts Aries' need for freedom, they can balance each other.";

"Aries is fiery, bold, and thrives on excitement in relationships. They are natural leaders who seek adventure and intensity, and they need a partner who can keep up with their passionate drive. While their energy is infectious, their impulsiveness can create tension with more cautious or sensitive signs." = "Aries is fiery, bold, and thrives on excitement in relationships. They are natural leaders who seek adventure and intensity, and they need a partner who can keep up with their passionate drive. While their energy is infectious, their impulsiveness can create tension with more cautious or sensitive signs.";

"Taurus is grounded, sensual, and values stability in relationships. They seek loyalty, comfort, and a steady rhythm with their partner. While patient and devoted, they may struggle with signs that crave too much change or unpredictability. Their ideal partner appreciates consistency and reliability, while still igniting Taurus' deep passions." = "Taurus is grounded, sensual, and values stability in relationships. They seek loyalty, comfort, and a steady rhythm with their partner. While patient and devoted, they may struggle with signs that crave too much change or unpredictability. Their ideal partner appreciates consistency and reliability, while still igniting Taurus' deep passions.";

